course: dictionary
lesson: 7504
title: Potential: what could be
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Potential means possible in the future, but not yet real. «It's got potential» is a polite way of saying a house is not nice now, but it could be with work and money.
explain: As a noun, potential is the ability or talent that could grow into success. «Not working to her full potential» is a polite way of saying she is lazy, because she is not using the talent she has.
explain: In science, potential energy is energy stored in something because of its position or shape, like a stretched spring or a book on a high shelf. When the book falls, that stored energy turns into moving energy.
fact: Potential is an adjective when it describes something: a potential danger is a danger that might happen.
fact: Potential is a noun when it names a talent: a pupil can have great potential.
fact: «Potential» means possible in the future, but not yet real.
fact: Potential energy is stored energy, from position or shape.
fact: Useful phrases: reach your potential, have potential, potential danger, potential energy.
exercise: «It's got potential.» What does this tell you about the house? | It is perfect and needs nothing at all | *It is not very nice now, but it could be with work and money | It is for sale only in the summer | It has no windows or doors
exercise: Ruby says the icy pond is a potential danger. What does potential mean here? | Very, very large | *Possible, but not certain yet | Stored inside a stretched spring | Definitely happening right now
exercise: What is potential energy? | Energy that is moving very fast | Energy from the sun only | *Energy stored because of position or shape | Energy that makes you feel sleepy
test: In «Not working to her full potential», what kind of word is potential? | An adjective | A verb | *A noun | A question word
test: A book on a high shelf has which kind of energy? | *Potential energy | Moving energy | Heat energy | Sound energy
exam: Which sentence uses potential as a noun? | *Mia has great potential as a dancer | The sign warns of a potential danger | The road is potential and wet | The ice may be potential
